  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "The shield stacks on the Due's headers. Only the pins the sketch and power need are drawn: PWM_A to D3, DIR_A to D12, BRAKE_A to D9, CURRENT_SENSE_A to A0, plus VIN and GND.",
   "The motor's two leads go into the channel A screw terminals. Which lead goes to + or - decides the 'forward' direction, and the manual doesn't say.",
   "The 12V wall wart goes into the Due's DC jack. VIN then feeds the shield and motor.",
   "The usb-cable has no ports in the catalogue, so its port is left null. The Due's USB port is assumed to be usb-micro. The Due's power-jack and usb-micro ports are taken from the Due catalogue card and assumed to exist on arduino-due-r3.",
   "The wall wart's sleeve (ground) is not drawn as a separate edge. The tip edge is used because the jack is a single port."
  ]
 },
